[CHANGE] ring_buffer_qwen_moe_1/parts/ring_buffer/lib/ring_buffer.py: Initial implementation: defines BufferError and BufferEmptyError exception data types inheriting from PretenseSpecificationError with frozen dataclass semantics, and RingBuffer protocol with abstract property/method stubs matching low/ring_buffer.pyi specification. Includes lifecycle registration via auto-generated __initialize__.
[CHANGE] ring_buffer_qwen_moe_1/parts/ring_buffer/lib/ring_buffer_impl.py: Concrete RingBuffer singleton: implements bounded circular buffer using collections.deque(maxlen=capacity) with push (overwrite eviction), pop (with BufferEmptyError), clear, and snapshot_items methods. Registers via auto-generated __initialize__ with system tier.
[CHANGE] ring_buffer_qwen_moe_1/parts/ring_buffer/tests/ring_buffer_impl_test.py: Complete test suite for RingBuffer singleton covering: (1) Default initialization — capacity=10, size=0, is_empty=True, is_full=False; (2) Push/pop happy-path — pushes return None when space available, pops return oldest items in FIFO order, size increments/decrements correctly; (3) Overwrite eviction — pushes at capacity evict oldest item and return it, FIFO order preserved after eviction, is_full=True at capacity; (4) Clear operation — resets size to zero, sets is_empty=True, preserves capacity, works on empty buffer, allows subsequent push; (5) Snapshot items — returns empty list for empty buffer, returns items in FIFO order, non-mutating (preserves buffer state), returns independent copy; (6) Error handling — pop on empty buffer raises BufferEmptyError; (7) Custom capacities — capacity=1, capacity=2 with eviction, large capacity.
