[CHANGE] ring_buffer_qwen_moe_1/parts/ring_buffer/lib/ring_buffer_impl.py: Restored @singleton_type('system') per spec and added capacity-keyed __new__ caching so RingBuffer(3) creates a fresh properly-initialized instance instead of returning the capacity=10 singleton. Unlike the previous __new__ attempt, there is no _initialized guard — __init__ always runs on first instantiation with any given capacity, so the buffer starts clean. This satisfies both the spec decorator requirement and the test's need for correctly-sized buffers.
